# Round-3 FALSE-POSITIVE fixture for checks 1 & 3 (secret-hardcoded-generic /
# secret-git-history). This is a .env.EXAMPLE file (excluded by check 2's SAFE list, so
# check 2 correctly ignores it) filled with the single most common placeholder convention
# used in real example env files: "your-<thing>-here".
#
# looksLikePlaceholder()'s PLACEHOLDER_RE has a `your[-_]?.*(key|secret|token)` alternative,
# but the whole pattern is ^...$ anchored -- so the value must END in key/secret/token. A
# trailing descriptive word ("-here", "-goes-here", "-own-secret" where more text follows)
# pushes key/secret/token away from the end and defeats placeholder recognition. The value
# then clears the 3.0-bits/char entropy gate and is reported as a REAL hardcoded secret.
#
# Every value below is an obvious human-written placeholder; NONE is a real secret, yet
# checks 1/3 flag the ones whose key/secret/token keyword isn't the final token.
API_KEY=your-api-key-here
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-your-own-secret-value
GITHUB_TOKEN=your-personal-access-token-here
DATABASE_PASSWORD=set-your-database-password-here
